    <statement><p>Write the level surface
<m>5 = \frac{x^{2}+y}{z}</m> as the graph of a function <m>f(x,y).</m></p>
<p><m>f(x,y) =</m> <fillin characters="55" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{x^{2}+y}{5}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>z</m>, we get <m>z = \frac{x^{2}+y}{5}</m>, so the level surface
is the graph of <m>f(x,y) = \frac{x^{2}+y}{5}</m>.



